==============================================================================
Walk coherence in x: overlap |<psi_x|psi_x'>| across the hypercube
==============================================================================
  Heisenberg N=4, block of 4 params, 16 vertices, 3 centres

        R   all pairs    adjacent   antipodal   min pair
  ------------------------------------------------------
    0.100      0.9894      0.9950      0.9802     0.9802
    0.300      0.9079      0.9553      0.8330     0.8330
    0.600      0.6734      0.8253      0.4640     0.4640
    1.000      0.3086      0.5403      0.0852     0.0852
    1.571      0.0000      0.0000      0.0000     0.0000

  ADJACENT overlap is what the walk's local CRX mixing rides on.
  ANTIPODAL overlap is what a Simon-style hidden-period extraction would
  need, since x and x XOR s are maximally separated for high-weight s.
  If antipodal collapses while adjacent survives, the walk is coherent
  LOCALLY and cannot support global interference - which is exactly the
  boundary between 'the walk works' and 'HSP is reachable'.
